        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಪಟ್ಟಣ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪಟ್ಟಣ — paṭṭaṇa — \"a small town; a town\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನನ್ನ ಊರು ಒಂದು ಚಿಕ್ಕ ಪಟ್ಟಣ. nanna ūru ondu cikka paṭṭaṇa. My home town is a small town."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ಪಟ್ಟಣಗಳು, paṭṭaṇagaḷu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Bigger than a ಹಳ್ಳಿ, smaller than a ನಗರ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪಟ್ಟಣ (paṭṭaṇa) comes from Sanskrit paṭṭana, \"a town\" (CDIAL 7705); Turner notes that the Sanskrit word itself was probably taken from a Dravidian source."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
